  "equipment_type": "Boiler outdoor reset control",
  "applies_to": "Heat-Timer HWR Platinum hot water reset control for a single burner or a motorized mixing valve, with the BACnet IP/MS/TP communication board.",
  "summary": "The HWR Platinum is an outdoor-reset control for one boiler burner or a motorized valve. With the BACnet board it exposes its settings and readings as Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values with instances in steps of 100. Most settings are writable from the BMS; the sensor readings, outputs and calculated target are read-only.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Objects are Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values only. Rows without a read-only mark in the manual are listed as writable.",
    "Temperature objects use °F or °C depending on the INMODE (sensor type/mode) setting.",
    "Start-up settings can be read but not written over BACnet; Heat-Timer says to set them at the panel first.",
    "The manual prints some rows as ranges (SCHEDULES00-55 = 2200-2255). Only the first and last printed objects of each range are listed here; the ones in between follow the same pattern.",
    "BOOST applies only when BOOSTMODE is Vari Boost or Vari Boost & ESD.",
    "Variable list: manual pages 8-9."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "The HWR runs its own outdoor reset. From the BMS, read the calculated target, system and outdoor temperatures and the burner/valve and pump outputs; adjust the reset with OFFSET, the reset ratio R or the minimum/maximum targets, and force a day/night shift if needed.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
